From: Ali Erdinc Koroglu <ali.koroglu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:06:18 +0300
Subject: build: drop REQUIRED from find_package(QCBOR)

QCBOR has been optional since the libcbor fallback landed, so REQUIRED
now states the opposite of the intent. It has no effect today only
because cmake/FindQCBOR.cmake sets QCBOR_FOUND by hand and never calls
find_package_handle_standard_args(), which is what would otherwise honor
REQUIRED and abort. Should that module ever be converted to the standard
helper, the fallback path would become unreachable

Signed-off-by: Ali Erdinc Koroglu <ali.koroglu@oss.qualcomm.com>

Origin: https://github.com/qualcomm/quic-teec/pull/30/commits/3bff0b4b6c203110ec6e919104f5e602945bc274
Forwarded: https://github.com/qualcomm/quic-teec/pull/30
Last-Update: 2026-10-07
---
 libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt b/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt
index adaef66..4bb508d 100644
--- a/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libqcomtee/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ list(APPEND CMAKE_MODULE_PATH "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/cmake")
 
 set(QCBOR_DIR_HINT "" CACHE PATH "Hint path for QCBOR directory")
 
-find_package(QCBOR REQUIRED)
+find_package(QCBOR)
 if(NOT QCBOR_FOUND)
 	message(WARNING "QCBOR not found, falling back to libcbor")
 endif()
